The schema is a `value` argument that can be either:
1. An array of arrays, where each inner array contains either strings or objects
2. An array of arrays, where each inner array contains numbers from enum [59, 62, 65]

The minimal valid value would be an empty array, since there's no minItems constraint mentioned. Let me check the schema again:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "value": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "anyOf": [
                {"type": "object"},
                {"type": "string"}
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "number",
              "enum": [59, 62, 65]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "required": ["value"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

An empty array `[]` satisfies both branches. So the minimal valid value is `{"value": []}`.
